# Run dumps are local noise — there are hundreds and they are reproducible from the
# .runs.jsonl beside them. Ignored by default.
*.json

# Except the handful that are evidence. A test opens each of these unguarded, and a document
# quotes figures from them, so a clean checkout has to have them or the test is a pass that only
# happens on the machine that produced the file. They are force-added; if you add another, add it
# here too. `test_published_figures.py` fails when a test names a result file the repo does not
# carry, which is how pilot-121.json was found after three tests had depended on it for weeks.
!pilot-121.json
!ladder-121-tools-holdout.json
!ladder-121-skills-pooled.json
!skill-baseline.json
